 ## Limitations

+- **VP9 decoder pool workaround (2026-10-08):** On this RTX 5070 Ti setup,
+  the portrait VP9 sample `DeH3GECqmsr` becomes dark and block-corrupted with
+  RTX HDR and a 50-surface D3D11 decoder pool (`backstep-cache=32`,
+  `hwdec-extra-frames=6`). Both plain D3D11 decoding and VPP without HDR are
+  clean. Reproducing with `backstep-cache=0` and `hwdec-extra-frames=38`
+  isolates the enlarged pool rather than stored backward frames. The
+  `on_loaded` hook in `rtx-video-auto.lua` caps the file-local backstep cache
+  at 16 for VP9 with `hwdec=d3d11va` (34 surfaces with the current settings),
+  retaining hardware decoding and RTX HDR. It runs before decoder creation;
+  automatic profiles observing `video-format` apply too late. Smaller user
+  limits are preserved, and mpv restores the configured size at file end.
+  This also fixes the VP9 sample `DeM1DA0RNTM`. This is a local workaround; the
+  underlying driver/filter defect and its exact surface limit are unconfirmed.
+  Verified with full playback of `DeM1DA0RNTM`, clean captures at 2/6/10/13
+  seconds, three backward-frame steps, and a VP9/H.264/VP9 transition restoring
+  cache sizes 16/32/16. All three Roaming Lua regression harnesses pass.
 - **D3D11 Only:** Does not work with Vulkan or OpenGL APIs.
 - **Hardware Decoding:** Prefer `hwdec=d3d11va`. `d3d11vpp` requests D3D11 surfaces; the `-copy` path downloads every frame to RAM. Keep `d3d11va-copy` only if zero-copy + VPP fails on the GPU.
 - **Single Instance:** Only one instance of the RTX Video filter is managed.
